  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 300 PM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nFor this afternoon, we are monitoring the development of isolated \nstrong to severe storms ahead of the cold front which is \ncurrently pushing into northern portions of the forecast area.\nOverall, the low/mid level lapse rates are not as favorable today\nfor severe microbursts with damaging winds, so expect less \ncoverage of intense convection as we go through the remainder of \nthe day. The official beginning of fall on the calendar is today,\nand this just happens to coincide with what will hopefully be \nthis year's last episode of \"dangerous heat\" in our area. While\nconditions will not remind one of fall, we can at least expect\nwhat would be considered more typical of September.\n\nLooking ahead for late this week and through the weekend, drier \nand \"less hot\" conditions will continue. Then by the time we get \nto the middle of next week, there may be a more signicant frontal \nboundary that pushes slowly into our region with sufficient \nmoisture and ascent for greater rain chances. /EC/",
